<title>UK: LME COPPER TOUCH EASIER IN LATE TRADING.</title>
<headline>LME COPPER TOUCH EASIER IN LATE TRADING.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>LME copper was barely weaker in late inter-office trading on Wednesday evening.</p>
<p>At 1800 GMT, three months copper was indicated at $2,285/$2,289 per tonne, compared to a kerb close of $2,290.</p>
<p>Prices ended the afternoon kerb $12 firmer, but well within its recent range, after LME inventories rose by a modest 50 tonnes.</p>
<p>The other metals were little changed.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542-8065</p>
